\chapter{VS-ACSE Scientific Validation}
\label{chap:vsacse_validation}

\section{Overview}

This chapter presents the complete scientific validation protocol for the
Venusian Sub-Surface Astrological Cryptographic Simulation Engine (VS-ACSE),
version VS-ACSE-v4.0-REV2026. The objective of the validation campaign is to
demonstrate strict hardware-deterministic execution, zero-allocation numerical
stability, AVX2 SIMD lane reproducibility, and cryptographic audit integrity
across one million discrete simulation epochs.

The validation confirms that VS-ACSE maintains exact bit-level consistency
across heterogeneous hardware nodes, ensuring that Venusian mantle-plume
dynamics, rift-flank widening trajectories, and cryptographically bound
telemetry states evolve deterministically under Q16.16 fixed-point arithmetic.

\section{Test Harness Configuration}

The validation harness was deployed on a page-locked, hard-aligned memory
substrate to eliminate OS paging jitter and garbage-collection interference.
The following configuration parameters were enforced:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Arithmetic Substrate:} Q16.16 fixed-point format using
    32-bit signed integers (16-bit integer, 16-bit fractional).
    \item \textbf{Vectorization Width:} 256-bit AVX2 SIMD registers operating
    on 8 parallel 32-bit lanes per \texttt{\_\_m256i} block.
    \item \textbf{Cryptographic Layer:} In-place ChaCha20 stream cipher with
    continuous step-level SHA3-256 hashing.
    \item \textbf{Epoch Count:} $N = 10^6$ simulation steps.
    \item \textbf{Cross-Node Migration:} Forced topology migration between
    heterogeneous nodes to test deterministic reproducibility.
\end{itemize}

All simulation steps were executed without heap allocation, ensuring that
memory locality and register pinning remained stable throughout the entire
validation run.

