\section{Deterministic Execution Theorem}

\textbf{Theorem 1 (Hardware-Deterministic Venusian Dynamics).}  
Under Q16.16 fixed-point arithmetic, AVX2 SIMD lane pinning, zero-allocation
memory constraints, and step-level SHA3-256 verification, the VS-ACSE engine
defines a deterministic mapping:

\[
\Phi_{\text{VS-ACSE}} :
\left(
\mathbf{S}(t_k), \Delta t_k
\right)
\mapsto
\mathbf{S}(t_{k+1})
\]

such that:

\[
\forall k,\quad
\mathbf{S}(t_{k+1})_{\text{node}_i}
